            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The complete body of the redeemed people of God, often specifically representing the union of Old and New Covenant believers (represented by the 12 Patriarchs and 12 Apostles), as well as spiritual maturity, wisdom, and pastoral authority.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Revelation 4:4\",\"Revelation 5:8-10\",\"1 Peter 5:1-5\",\"Acts 20:17-28\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"An exalted order of angelic beings or a heavenly divine council assisting in God's governance.\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 89:7\",\"Isaiah 24:23\",\"Revelation 7:11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"},{\"meaning\":\"Exclusively Old Testament saints or literal national Israel.\",\"basis\":[\"Hebrews 11:2\"],\"prominence\":\"rare\"},{\"meaning\":\"Literal local church leadership and pastoral authority without symbolic application.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Timothy 5:17\",\"Titus 1:5\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"In apocalyptic literature, particularly the Book of Revelation, the 'twenty-four elders' are overwhelmingly interpreted symbolically in Christian tradition as the glorified Church or the entirety of God's redeemed people. In other contexts, the term functions less symbolically and more literally to represent wisdom, spiritual maturity, and delegated pastoral authority.\"}",
